\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{One-vertex marginals with many extensions}
\date{2026-11-01}

\p{Compatibility of [local Gaussian data](fdip-0064) alone does not
imply uniqueness. On the cover
#{\{0\},\{1\}} of two vertices, prescribe a standard normal law at
each vertex. Every covariance
##{G_\rho=\begin{pmatrix}1&\rho\\\rho&1\end{pmatrix},
\qquad -1<\rho<1,}
is a positive-definite global extension. The product law is the member
#{\rho=0}. Uniqueness will require an additional conditional-independence
condition.}
